WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.496 --> 00:00:16.198
she was at Aunt March's, Amy felt as though she were trapped in a pitch-black tunnel with no

2
00:00:16.258 --> 00:00:17.839
light beckoning to her at the end.

3
00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:23.841
Until then, Amy had taken for granted the liveliness and warm affection of her family.

4
00:00:24.882 --> 00:00:30.044
How she missed the constant cheerful voices that seemed to fill the whole house all day long.

5
00:00:31.848 --> 00:00:33.450
"Did I ask you to stop?"

6
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.673
Aunt March snapped when Amy, who was reading to her, paused to think about her family.

7
00:00:37.693 --> 00:00:42.417
"Stop!" screeched Polly as she took the cracker Aunt March offered her.

8
00:00:42.437 --> 00:00:44.519
"Forgive me, Aunt March.

9
00:00:44.979 --> 00:00:48.502
I'll continue said Amy, returning her attention to the story.

10
00:00:49.643 --> 00:00:53.126
Aunt March might have been a nasty woman but she was not heartless.

11
00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:59.592
She was also worried about the fate of Beth, who she thought was witless but pure-hearted and innocent.

12
00:01:00.308 --> 00:01:02.109
"What have you heard about your sister?"

13
00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:04.609
This time she interrupted Amy's reading.

14
00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:10.751
Fiddling with a corner of the page she was reading, Amy replied, "Laurie says that Beth is coping

15
00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:15.472
better but her fever still has to drop, and she remains stable but weak."

16
00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:17.533
"And what of your Father?

17
00:01:17.913 --> 00:01:19.373
Will he be coming home soon?"

18
00:01:19.853 --> 00:01:20.553
asked Aunt March.

19
00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:28.056
Shaking her head, Amy said tearfully, "According to the last message we got, Father doesn't have the strength

20
00:01:28.096 --> 00:01:29.536
yet to make the journey home."

21
00:01:30.672 --> 00:01:35.994
"Rubbish! Your sister needs your mother more than he does," Aunt March remarked in a gruff voice.

22
00:01:36.014 --> 00:01:41.737
"Hannah says it's best not to tell Mother just yet, since there isn't much she can do here

23
00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:43.077
anyway," said Amy.

24
00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:48.879
Aunt March felt a pang in her heart as she watched Amy struggle to control her emotions.

25
00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.161
"I have a gift for you," she said in a kinder voice.

26
00:01:54.242 --> 00:02:00.104
Amy, wiping her tears (with a silk handkerchief, like a true lady), turned to her with curiosity.

27
00:02:01.124 --> 00:02:05.909
Aunt March held out a small green velvety box, which Amy slowly took from her.

28
00:02:05.929 --> 00:02:08.332
"Oh, Aunt March!

29
00:02:08.752 --> 00:02:14.318
I can't accept this," gasped Amy, holding up an emerald ring that flashed brilliantly in the light.

30
00:02:15.179 --> 00:02:20.344
"Yes, you can and you will, because I am giving it to you," Aunt March replied in a

31
00:02:20.424 --> 00:02:24.048
firm and strict voice that meant Amy should not try to argue with her.

32
00:02:25.196 --> 00:02:31.299
"It's beautiful," Amy said, her eyes dancing joyously as she put the ring on her middle finger.

33
00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:33.340
"I'm glad you like it.

34
00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:37.823
Now get back to the story," snapped Aunt March as she fed Polly another cracker.

35
00:02:38.944 --> 00:02:44.306
In addition to the ring, Aunt March promised Amy many more gifts as long as she remained obedient

36
00:02:44.386 --> 00:02:46.328
and found favor in the old lady's eyes.

37
00:02:47.928 --> 00:02:53.772
Upon his next daily visit, Amy promptly told this all to Laurie, who looked doubtful as he listened

38
00:02:53.832 --> 00:03:00.238
patiently. "Aunt March says emeralds are the most precious gems in the world," Amy said, sticking her hand

39
00:03:00.298 --> 00:03:01.298
out for him to admire.

40
00:03:01.318 --> 00:03:06.159
"It's very lovely, but don't you think you're a little too young for that?"

41
00:03:06.499 --> 00:03:07.560
asked Laurie with a frown.

42
00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:12.781
"Age means nothing if you are a true lady," Amy said knowingly.

43
00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:17.983
"Aunt March says I have the potential to become a respected woman of society."

44
00:03:18.983 --> 00:03:24.274
Laurie mumbled his opinion of Aunt March under his breath, but apparently Amy still had much more to

45
00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:25.775
say about material things.

46
00:03:25.795 --> 00:03:32.000
"Aunt March says I'm to have her pearl necklace, earrings, and diamond brooch after she dies!"

47
00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.542
"So you want her to die, do you?"

48
00:03:34.882 --> 00:03:36.163
Laurie asked nastily.

49
00:03:36.844 --> 00:03:39.146
Reddening in the face, Amy stuttered, "No.

50
00:03:39.826 --> 00:03:43.509
What I meant was "Do you want to know how Beth is or not?"

51
00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:45.211
Laurie asked rather harshly.

52
00:03:46.271 --> 00:03:51.315
Caught up in her own fantasy world, Amy had forgotten at that moment why Laurie was visiting her

53
00:03:51.375 --> 00:03:51.836
every day.

54
00:03:52.796 --> 00:03:55.518
"Of course, Laurie," she said, shamefaced.

55
00:03:56.698 --> 00:04:00.461
"Well, Beth is still Laurie began more gently.

56
00:04:01.121 --> 00:04:03.462
As he spoke, Amy looked down at the ring.

57
00:04:04.303 --> 00:04:09.106
It didn't seem to shine as beautifully anymore, nor did the thought of a pearl necklace seem so

58
00:04:09.166 --> 00:04:15.589
appealing. The reality was that Beth was gravely sick, and death was no joking matter.

59
00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.752
After Laurie had left, Amy had a lot to think about.

60
00:04:20.712 --> 00:04:23.693
She stared at herself in the mirror for a very long time.

61
00:04:24.753 --> 00:04:29.494
Speaking to her reflection, Amy said, "One day you're going to die, too."

62
00:04:29.514 --> 00:04:32.935
"Can I take these things with me to my grave?"

63
00:04:33.275 --> 00:04:33.816
she wondered.

64
00:04:34.856 --> 00:04:40.017
Struck by the truth, she was forced to realize that her possessions would have no value to her

65
00:04:40.137 --> 00:04:40.917
once she were dead.

66
00:04:41.878 --> 00:04:47.279
After much soul searching, Amy decided to write a will, reasoning, "I want the people I love to

67
00:04:47.339 --> 00:04:50.080
have my things so they'll remember me by them."

68
00:04:51.096 --> 00:04:58.120
Armed with pen and paper, Amy began to write her last will and testament: I, Amy Curtis March,

69
00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:05.884
being of sound mind, do give all my possessions to the following persons named: To Father, all my

70
00:05:05.944 --> 00:05:11.467
drawings and sketches—those I kept since I was a little girl up to the ones he never saw.

71
00:05:12.888 --> 00:05:17.470
To Mother, all my clothes, except for the blue dress with pink and white flowers.

72
00:05:18.271 --> 00:05:19.791
That one I want Kitty to have.

73
00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:20.712
See below.

74
00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:26.884
To Meg, I give the emerald ring from Aunt March, because it is the perfect match for the

75
00:05:26.945 --> 00:05:27.985
color of your eyes.

76
00:05:28.866 --> 00:05:30.568
The velvet box I also give.

77
00:05:31.748 --> 00:05:36.813
To Jo, I give you all my hair ribbons so that when your hair grows long again, you

78
00:05:36.853 --> 00:05:39.735
will have beautiful, colorful ribbons to decorate it with.

79
00:05:40.636 --> 00:05:43.999
I also give you all my pens for you to write more stories with.

80
00:05:44.759 --> 00:05:51.736
To Beth (if she survives), all my dolls, my little play set of teacups, and pink slippers.

81
00:05:52.957 --> 00:05:58.958
To Laurie, I leave you my handkerchiefs with my initials embroidered on them so you will always remember

82
00:05:59.018 --> 00:06:00.219
me as a true lady.

83
00:06:01.079 --> 00:06:01.599
To Mr.

84
00:06:01.659 --> 00:06:04.540
Laurence, I give you my sculptures of your horses.

85
00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:09.621
I especially loved Harris, and there are two paintings of him that I hope you like.

86
00:06:10.462 --> 00:06:16.703
To Kitty Bryant, my blue dress with pink flowers and my bead necklace, which she always admired.

87
00:06:17.724 --> 00:06:21.925
To Hannah, my collection of seashells and the purple box I kept them in.

88
00:06:22.866 --> 00:06:27.968
And now, after leaving my possessions in the care of those I love and trust, I want to

89
00:06:28.048 --> 00:06:32.930
say how much I love you all and that each one of you has a special place in

90
00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:33.490
my heart.

91
00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.891
I trust we shall meet again.

92
00:06:36.571 --> 00:06:45.115
Signed: Amy Curtis March When Amy finished writing her will, a peaceful calm came over her.

93
00:06:46.315 --> 00:06:52.933
She prayed, "God, if you allow Beth to live, I promise to be a better sister, daughter, and

94
00:06:53.033 --> 00:06:57.975
friend. Please give me the opportunity to prove that I have really changed."

95
00:06:58.995 --> 00:07:03.536
The next day when Laurie came, Amy showed him the will and asked him to sign it as

96
00:07:03.576 --> 00:07:04.036
a witness.

97
00:07:05.017 --> 00:07:08.918
Amused yet touched by Amy's maturity and thoughtfulness, Laurie agreed.

98
00:07:10.038 --> 00:07:11.539
Then he gave Amy the good news.

99
00:07:12.479 --> 00:07:14.920
"Mother March is coming home soon," he announced.

100
00:07:16.704 --> 00:07:20.066
"Beth? Does that mean Amy couldn't even say the words.

101
00:07:21.046 --> 00:07:25.369
Laurie took a deep breath and said, "I don't know, but Dr.

102
00:07:25.409 --> 00:07:26.929
Bangs said to send for your mother.

103
00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:29.051
The girls don't know yet.

104
00:07:29.371 --> 00:07:30.651
I want it to be a surprise."

105
00:07:31.732 --> 00:07:33.993
Amy was overjoyed that Mother was returning.

106
00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:38.896
She wondered whether her homecoming would be a happy or sad one.
